  "content": {
    "id": "p57-q1-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "1",
    "prompt": "Prove these identities.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p57-q1-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$(x+5)(x-5)+25=x^2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Expand the LHS: $x^2-25+25=x^2=\\mathrm{RHS}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\mathrm{LHS}&=(x+5)(x-5)+25\\\\&=x^2-25+25\\\\&=x^2\\\\&=\\mathrm{RHS}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p57-q1-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$(x+4)^2-16=x(x+8)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Expand and factorise the LHS: $x^2+8x=x(x+8)=\\mathrm{RHS}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\mathrm{LHS}&=(x+4)^2-16\\\\&=x^2+8x+16-16\\\\&=x^2+8x\\\\&=x(x+8)\\\\&=\\mathrm{RHS}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 31
      },
      {
        "id": "p57-q1-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$(x+3)^2-(x-3)^2=12x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Expand both squares on the LHS and simplify to $12x=\\mathrm{RHS}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\mathrm{LHS}&=(x+3)^2-(x-3)^2\\\\&=(x^2+6x+9)-(x^2-6x+9)\\\\&=x^2+6x+9-x^2+6x-9\\\\&=12x\\\\&=\\mathrm{RHS}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      },
      {
        "id": "p57-q1-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$(a+b)^2-(a-b)^2=4ab$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Expand both squares on the LHS and simplify to $4ab=\\mathrm{RHS}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\mathrm{LHS}&=(a+b)^2-(a-b)^2\\\\&=(a^2+2ab+b^2)-(a^2-2ab+b^2)\\\\&=a^2+2ab+b^2-a^2+2ab-b^2\\\\&=4ab\\\\&=\\mathrm{RHS}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      },
      {
        "id": "p57-q1-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$(x+h)^2-x^2=h(2x+h)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Expand and factorise the LHS: $2xh+h^2=h(2x+h)=\\mathrm{RHS}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\mathrm{LHS}&=(x+h)^2-x^2\\\\&=x^2+2xh+h^2-x^2\\\\&=2xh+h^2\\\\&=h(2x+h)\\\\&=\\mathrm{RHS}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 31
      },
      {
        "id": "p57-q1-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$x^2+2x+1-(x+1)=x(x+1)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Factorise the LHS: $(x+1)[(x+1)-1]=x(x+1)=\\mathrm{RHS}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\mathrm{LHS}&=x^2+2x+1-(x+1)\\\\&=(x+1)^2-(x+1)\\\\&=(x+1)[(x+1)-1]\\\\&=(x+1)x\\\\&=x(x+1)\\\\&=\\mathrm{RHS}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      },
      {
        "id": "p57-q1-g",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "g",
        "prompt": "$x^3-x=x(x-1)(x+1)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Factorise the LHS: $x(x^2-1)=x(x-1)(x+1)=\\mathrm{RHS}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\mathrm{LHS}&=x^3-x\\\\&=x(x^2-1)\\\\&=x(x-1)(x+1)\\\\&=\\mathrm{RHS}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p57-q1-h",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "h",
        "prompt": "$x^2+6x+5=(x+3)^2-4$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Expand the RHS: $x^2+6x+9-4=x^2+6x+5=\\mathrm{LHS}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\mathrm{RHS}&=(x+3)^2-4\\\\&=x^2+6x+9-4\\\\&=x^2+6x+5\\\\&=\\mathrm{LHS}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p57-q1-i",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "i",
        "prompt": "$3x^2-6x+5=3(x-1)^2+2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Expand the RHS and simplify to $3x^2-6x+5=\\mathrm{LHS}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\mathrm{RHS}&=3(x-1)^2+2\\\\&=3(x^2-2x+1)+2\\\\&=3x^2-6x+3+2\\\\&=3x^2-6x+5\\\\&=\\mathrm{LHS}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 31
      },
      {
        "id": "p57-q1-j",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "j",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{x^2+x}{x}=x+1,\\quad x\\ne0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Factorise and cancel: $\\dfrac{x(x+1)}{x}=x+1=\\mathrm{RHS}$, since $x\\ne0$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\mathrm{LHS}&=\\frac{x^2+x}{x}\\\\&=\\frac{x(x+1)}{x}\\\\&=x+1\\\\&=\\mathrm{RHS}\\end{align*}$$\nCancellation is valid because $x\\ne0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 35
      },
      {
        "id": "p57-q1-k",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "k",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac1x+\\dfrac1{x+1}=\\dfrac{2x+1}{x(x+1)},\\quad x\\ne0,-1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Use denominator $x(x+1)$: $\\dfrac{x+1+x}{x(x+1)}=\\dfrac{2x+1}{x(x+1)}=\\mathrm{RHS}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\mathrm{LHS}&=\\frac1x+\\frac1{x+1}\\\\&=\\frac{x+1}{x(x+1)}+\\frac{x}{x(x+1)}\\\\&=\\frac{x+1+x}{x(x+1)}\\\\&=\\frac{2x+1}{x(x+1)}\\\\&=\\mathrm{RHS}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 51
      },
      {
        "id": "p57-q1-l",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "l",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac1{1-x}-\\dfrac1{1+x}=\\dfrac{2x}{1-x^2},\\quad x\\ne\\pm1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Use denominator $(1-x)(1+x)$ and simplify the numerator to $2x$, giving the RHS.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\mathrm{LHS}&=\\frac1{1-x}-\\frac1{1+x}\\\\&=\\frac{1+x}{(1-x)(1+x)}-\\frac{1-x}{(1-x)(1+x)}\\\\&=\\frac{(1+x)-(1-x)}{(1-x)(1+x)}\\\\&=\\frac{2x}{1-x^2}\\\\&=\\mathrm{RHS}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 55
      },
      {
        "id": "p58-m",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "m",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{x+1}{x-1}-\\dfrac{x-1}{x+1}=\\dfrac{4x}{x^2-1},\\quad x\\ne\\pm1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Use denominator $x^2-1$; the numerator becomes $(x+1)^2-(x-1)^2=4x$, giving the RHS.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\mathrm{LHS}&=\\frac{x+1}{x-1}-\\frac{x-1}{x+1}\\\\&=\\frac{(x+1)^2}{(x-1)(x+1)}-\\frac{(x-1)^2}{(x-1)(x+1)}\\\\&=\\frac{(x+1)^2-(x-1)^2}{x^2-1}\\\\&=\\frac{(x^2+2x+1)-(x^2-2x+1)}{x^2-1}\\\\&=\\frac{4x}{x^2-1}\\\\&=\\mathrm{RHS}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 68
      },
      {
        "id": "p58-n",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "n",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{1+x}{1-x}-\\dfrac{1-x}{1+x}=\\dfrac{4x}{1-x^2},\\quad x\\ne\\pm1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Use denominator $1-x^2$; the numerator becomes $(1+x)^2-(1-x)^2=4x$, giving the RHS.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\mathrm{LHS}&=\\frac{1+x}{1-x}-\\frac{1-x}{1+x}\\\\&=\\frac{(1+x)^2}{(1-x)(1+x)}-\\frac{(1-x)^2}{(1-x)(1+x)}\\\\&=\\frac{(1+x)^2-(1-x)^2}{1-x^2}\\\\&=\\frac{(1+2x+x^2)-(1-2x+x^2)}{1-x^2}\\\\&=\\frac{4x}{1-x^2}\\\\&=\\mathrm{RHS}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 68
      },
      {
        "id": "p58-o",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "o",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{x^2-4}{x^2+2x}=1-\\dfrac2x,\\quad x\\ne0,-2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Factorise and cancel $x+2$: $\\dfrac{x-2}{x}=1-\\dfrac2x=\\mathrm{RHS}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\mathrm{LHS}&=\\frac{x^2-4}{x^2+2x}\\\\&=\\frac{(x-2)(x+2)}{x(x+2)}\\\\&=\\frac{x-2}{x}\\\\&=\\frac{x}{x}-\\frac2x\\\\&=1-\\frac2x\\\\&=\\mathrm{RHS}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 54
      },
      {
        "id": "p58-p",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "p",
        "prompt": "$x+\\dfrac1x+2=\\dfrac{(x+1)^2}{x},\\quad x\\ne0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Expand the RHS and divide each term by $x$ to obtain $x+2+\\dfrac1x=\\mathrm{LHS}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\mathrm{RHS}&=\\frac{(x+1)^2}{x}\\\\&=\\frac{x^2+2x+1}{x}\\\\&=\\frac{x^2}{x}+\\frac{2x}{x}+\\frac1x\\\\&=x+2+\\frac1x\\\\&=\\mathrm{LHS}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 45
      },
      {
        "id": "p58-q",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "q",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{x^2+1}{x+1}-(x-1)=\\dfrac2{x+1},\\quad x\\ne-1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Use denominator $x+1$; the numerator becomes $x^2+1-(x^2-1)=2$, giving the RHS.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\mathrm{LHS}&=\\frac{x^2+1}{x+1}-(x-1)\\\\&=\\frac{x^2+1}{x+1}-\\frac{(x-1)(x+1)}{x+1}\\\\&=\\frac{x^2+1-(x^2-1)}{x+1}\\\\&=\\frac2{x+1}\\\\&=\\mathrm{RHS}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 53
      },
      {
        "id": "p58-r",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "r",
        "prompt": "$\\left(\\dfrac{x}{x+1}\\right)^2+\\dfrac1{(x+1)^2}=\\dfrac{x^2+1}{(x+1)^2},\\quad x\\ne-1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Square the fraction, then add over $(x+1)^2$ to obtain $\\dfrac{x^2+1}{(x+1)^2}=\\mathrm{RHS}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\mathrm{LHS}&=\\left(\\frac{x}{x+1}\\right)^2+\\frac1{(x+1)^2}\\\\&=\\frac{x^2}{(x+1)^2}+\\frac1{(x+1)^2}\\\\&=\\frac{x^2+1}{(x+1)^2}\\\\&=\\mathrm{RHS}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      }
    ]
  },
